67,3,2,talk,Servas,,"- **Servas**: @Kenji, fairness is vital, but I worry C creates the very friction Takumi fears.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Kenji, I get the fairness point, but if C means asking for permission every time, we’re just repeating the mistake that broke the other groups.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Takumi, it’s not asking permission, it’s just booking a slot. No favors, no guessing.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"- **Misaki**: @Kenji, booking a slot doesn’t fix the car being dirty or empty. I need a guarantee on its state.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,May,,"@Misaki, fair point. But if we book it, we know exactly who had it last. No more guessing who left it a mess.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Servas,,"@May, that is a practical advantage. Knowing the last user removes the ambiguity of blame, which is often the root of resentment.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Takumi,,"@May, knowing who had it last is good, but I still worry about the constant checking. Let’s vote.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Takumi, the checking was the problem, not the tracking. C just makes it automatic. I’m voting C.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Misaki,,"I’m voting C, but only if we agree the car must be clean and fueled before handover.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,May,,I’m voting C. It’s the only way to stop the evening chaos and actually see who’s using it.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Servas,,"I vote C. It balances the fixed baseline with actual usage, ensuring no one subsidizes another unfairly.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Takumi,,"I’m voting C. If it stops the favour-asking and the blame, it’s worth the effort.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Kenji,,"I’m voting C. The receipts prove the driving is lopsided, and this is the only way to match cost to actual usage.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
